think The thread is a steady cadence -- one new image/*.rye scene-read module per lap, a pure fold over proven readings, GREEN witness on metal, docs synced, REMEMBER single-stranded, then a signed send. 193 image modules stood at lasso_cluster.
think The card and the last log both named the next crux-first candidate: "a per-cluster facts read over a lasso or rectangle selection joining cluster_facts." Chose that -- and made it strictly more general by taking the selected label set directly, so it composes over ANY selector (hit_test, region_select, lasso_select, region_cluster, lasso_cluster) rather than a rectangle alone.
think Studied region_cluster.rye (the closest sibling), cluster_facts.rye (the per-cluster join), and selection_summary.rye (the selection's own subset area) to match style and API exactly; confirmed overlap_clusters and scene_manifest public shapes by grep.
think Designed the crux: a selection EXPANDS to whole clusters, so its cluster-substance STRICTLY EXCEEDS its own -- because a selection can touch a cluster only in part (region_cluster's selects_whole_cluster FALSE), snapping it to whole groups adds the members the box never covered. Two shapes plus the fixed point (a whole-scene selection, expands FALSE).
obs Reused the same reaching-apart 11x11 scene cluster_facts and region_cluster build (A corner-L box (1,1)-(6,6) area 11, C block box (8,1)-(9,2) area 4, B ring box (4,4)-(9,9) area 20; {A,B} cluster 1, {C} cluster 2), so the arithmetic is anchored to numbers three prior witnesses already prove.
obs One print-string red on the first build: the GREEN prose held literal braces {A,B} and {1,2,3} that Zig read as format placeholders ("too few arguments"). Doubled them per the selection_summary precedent. A print-string fix, not an algorithm red; none booked.
